Wait - "GOT WINDOW QUERY, responding" only printed ONCE. But there are TWO `\x1b[18t` in the data (one at the start of the level 0 screen, one at the end). The `responded` flag prevents the second response!

The issue: the first `\x1b[18t` was in the level 0 data, and I responded. But then the server sends ANOTHER `\x1b[18t` for the next level, and my `responded` flag is still True, so I don't respond.

I need to reset the `responded` flag, or better, respond to EVERY `\x1b[18t`. Let me remove the `responded` flag and just respond every time I see a new `\x1b[18t`.

Actually, the cleanest approach: track the position of the last `\x1b[18t` I responded to, and respond to any new one.


